# Per-project override of the base branch `devbrain execute` uses (instead of the
# repo's actual git default branch). One `project=branch` per line.
# Adding a line here is a deliberate act, same convention as devbrain-projects.allow.
#
# Use this when you want devbrain's PRs to land on a staging/preview branch instead
# of your real default branch, and you promote that branch to production yourself
# as a separate, deliberate step.
#
# Example (remove the leading '#' to enable):
# example-repo=develop
